====================================================================================================
D1 EXPERIMENT — ARCHITECTURE 1 (Apache Flink) — WATERMARK ALLOWANCE vs IMPUTATION
Summary across all three live runs (0s / 5s / 10s out-of-orderness allowance)
====================================================================================================
Each run replayed the same 5 disordered device streams (missing_timestamp_data/) through Flink
with a different forBoundedOutOfOrderness allowance.  "Imputed" rows are mean-fills inserted by
dataPreparation after Flink dropped out-of-order events (computed_value = YES in the device logs);
"real" rows are genuine sensor readings (computed_value = NO).

All three live runs side by side
--------------------------------

  ┌───────────┬────────────┬─────────┬───────────┐
  │ Allowance │ Total rows │ Imputed │ Imputed % │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼─────────┼───────────┤
  │ 0s        │      2 700 │     785 │    29.1 % │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼─────────┼───────────┤
  │ 5s        │      3 000 │     865 │    28.8 % │
  ├───────────┼────────────┼─────────┼───────────┤
  │ 10s       │      2 700 │     776 │    28.7 % │
  └───────────┴────────────┴─────────┴───────────┘

